<br />input variables,</p>
        <p begin="00:00:21.080" end="00:00:25.320" tts:direction="ltr">whether we were using those DataTables or
<br />Goal seek or our</p>
        <p begin="00:00:25.320" end="00:00:30.840" tts:direction="ltr">scenario manager in order to understand
<br />how inputs would change an output.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:30.840" end="00:00:33.120" tts:direction="ltr">We're going to do something extremely</p>
        <p begin="00:00:33.120" end="00:00:35.640" tts:direction="ltr">similar this week with something called
<br />Solver.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:35.640" end="00:00:38.840" tts:direction="ltr">And what Solver lets you do is really
<br />actually</p>
        <p begin="00:00:38.840" end="00:00:42.600" tts:direction="ltr">quite cool because Instead of just looking
<br />at</p>
        <p begin="00:00:42.600" end="00:00:46.600" tts:direction="ltr">one input variable or two input variables
<br />or setting</p>
        <p begin="00:00:46.600" end="00:00:51.400" tts:direction="ltr">a very specific set of inputs with
<br />scenario Manager,</p>
        <p begin="00:00:51.400" end="00:00:55.200" tts:direction="ltr">what Solver does is it actually lets you
<br />add constraints.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:55.200" end="00:00:56.760" tts:direction="ltr">So a lot of times in business,</p>
        <p begin="00:00:56.760" end="00:00:59.240" tts:direction="ltr">we have these operational constraints or
<br />constraints</p>
        <p begin="00:00:59.240" end="00:01:01.840" tts:direction="ltr">we've identified from our business in the
<br />past,</p>
        <p begin="00:01:01.840" end="00:01:05.840" tts:direction="ltr">so we're able to apply that extra layer on
